From 74c53d205ff475cf53333885a78f151601f622af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:29:09 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Degoogle: Google-service default preferences (translate
 offer, sign-in, FRE metrics)

The three Google-facing defaults that cromite sets in Modify-default-preferences
(dropped from our subset because it mixes in unrelated defaults):

- translate::prefs::kOfferTranslateEnabled defaults to false. Translation is
  already impossible in this tree (cromite's
  ungoogled-chromium-Disable-translate-integration makes
  TranslateManager::FilterIsTranslatePossible() refuse and removes the
  translate settings), so this only stops the pref from claiming otherwise.
- prefs::kSigninAllowed defaults to false: "Allow Chrome sign-in" is off and
  the dead NTP identity button no longer invites a sign-in that cannot happen
  without GMS.
- The first-run flow no longer opts the user into usage/crash reporting: the
  FRE footer loses its "Chrome sends usage and crash data to Google" sentence
  and "Help improve Chrome's features and performance" starts off. Metrics
  upload is compiled out anyway (Disable-various-metrics); this only stops the
  UI from claiming the opposite.

Found by the runtime UI test (testing/RUNTIME_UI.md, F3/F6).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
